<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Domingos José Martins</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1781">1781</a>–<a href="/years/1817">1817</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Domingos José Martins was a Brazilian merchant and one of the leaders of the Pernambucan Revolt of 1817 against Portuguese rule. As a member of the provisional government of the Republic of Pernambuco he helped abolish some taxes and proclaim freedom of conscience and the press. When royal forces crushed the revolt he was captured and executed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/domingos-jose-martins.jpg" alt="Domingos José Martins" width="320" height="379" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: M. J. Garnier · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Domingos_Martins.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
